<%# One chat line. Rendered three ways and it has to be one file: the page loop,
    the submitter's create.turbo_stream.erb, and Tv::StreamChat's after_create_commit
    broadcast to everyone else watching. The broadcast used to rely on implicit
    to_partial_path, which resolved to tv/stream_chats/_stream_chat — this file,
    which did not exist — so the enqueued job raised MissingTemplate and nobody but
    the sender ever saw a new message. %>
<p id="<%= dom_id(stream_chat) %>">
  <%= tag.strong stream_chat.author&.display_name || t("chat.anon") %>
  <%= time_tag stream_chat.created_at, l(stream_chat.created_at, format: "%H:%M") %>
  <%= stream_chat.message %>
</p>
